\doxysubsubsection{\texorpdfstring{compute\_voltage()}{compute\_voltage()}}
{\footnotesize\ttfamily \label{classDCff_a21d3686534b57e8534d15667cab06882} 
double DCff\+::compute\+\_\+voltage (\begin{DoxyParamCaption}\item[{double}]{alpha}{, }\item[{double}]{omega}{}\end{DoxyParamCaption}) const\hspace{0.3cm}{\ttfamily [inline]}}



Computes the voltage needed to achieve desired acceleration and velocity. 

Calculates the control voltage using the feedforward model\+: u = K\+\_\+a \texorpdfstring{$\ast$}{*} alpha + K\+\_\+v \texorpdfstring{$\ast$}{*} omega + K\+\_\+s \texorpdfstring{$\ast$}{*} sign(omega) where K\+\_\+a accounts for acceleration torque, K\+\_\+v for back-\/\+EMF, and K\+\_\+s for static friction. The sign function ensures friction opposes motion.


\begin{DoxyParams}[1]{Parameters}
\mbox{\texttt{in}}  & {\em alpha} & Desired angular acceleration in rad/s\texorpdfstring{$^\wedge$}{\string^}2 \\
\hline
\mbox{\texttt{in}}  & {\em omega} & Current angular velocity in rad/s\\
\hline
\end{DoxyParams}
\begin{DoxyReturn}{Returns}
Required voltage in volts to achieve the desired acceleration 
\end{DoxyReturn}


